d and to match the control's behavior. On both states the chip exposes name Status, role menuitem with a menubar parent (a valid required parent), expanded flipping from false to true and haspopup=menu; Enter and Space open a role=menu popup, focus moves inside it, and Escape closes it and returns focus to the chip. 1.3.1 and 2.1.1 are met because the structure is valid and the keyboard works. A button with aria-haspopup would be the more usual choice, but that is a best practice, not an A or AA failure."}
